===Etymology 1===
Attested very rarely and late, earliest in the 59 {{BCE}} "Slave's Contract" ({{lang|zh|《僮約》}}) by {{w|Wang Bao}} ({{lw|zh|王褒 (汉朝)|王褒}}) (Wang et al., 2008):<ref name = "WGK-2008">{{cite-journal|author1= Wang, Jin-Xiu|author2= Gao, Tian-Gang|work=  Annals of Botany|author3= Knapp, Sandra|year= 2008|title= Ancient Chinese literature reveals pathways of eggplant domestication|titleurl= https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2712397/|volume= 102|number= 6|pages= 891–897|page= 893}}</ref>
* {{zh-x|二-月 春分，…… 別 茄 披 蔥。|In the second month of the year, the Spring Equinox {{...}} separate and transplant seedlings of '''eggplant''' and scallion.|CL|ref='''59 {{BCE}}''',{{lw|zh|s:Page:Gujin_Tushu_Jicheng,_Volume_330_(1700-1725).djvu/83|僮約|pref=《|suf=》}} ("Slave's Contract") by {{lw|zh|王褒 (汉朝)|王褒}} ({{w|Wang Bao}}); English translation by Wang et al. (2008)<ref name = "WGK-2008"/>|collapsed=y}}

Alves (2022) relates this to {{cog|mkh-vie-pro|*gaː}} (whence {{cog|vi|cà}}), which he considers an early Chinese loanword.<ref name = "Alves-2022">{{cite-journal|work= Vietnamese: Linguistics: State of the Field|series= JSEALS Special Publication|seriesvolume= 9|author= Alves, Mark|year= 2022|title= Lexical Evidence of the Vietic Household Before and After Language Contact with Sinitic|titleurl= https://www.academia.edu/77897041/Lexical_Evidence_of_the_Vietic_Household_Before_and_After_Language_Contact_with_Sinitic|page= 48-49|pages= 15-58}}</ref><!--- However, the loan direction could also have been in reverse: i.e. from Proto-Vietic into Late Old Chinese.--->

