===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|うばら}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|sort=うばら|-}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref name="DJR">{{R:Daijirin}}</ref>  Used in the ''{{w|Man'yōshū}}'', completed some time after 759 CE.<ref>{{RQ:Manyoshu|16|3832}}, text [https://web.archive.org/web/20220626150734/http://jti.lib.virginia.edu/japanese/manyoshu/Man16Yo.html#3832 here]</ref>

Appears alongside the ''umara'' form (see below), suggesting possible {{w|Prenasalized consonant|prenasalization}}, perhaps realized as *{{IPAchar|/umbara/}}.

[[supersede|Superseded]] by ''ibara'' above.

